    "reasoning": "The dominant failure (6/8) is dismissing meta-options. The agent needs explicit guidance to treat meta-options as serious candidates. When a meta-option exists, the agent should ask: could the true result be strictly stronger than every concrete option listed? The secondary failure (2/8) involves the agent fabricating plausible-sounding arguments for why a weaker statement is 'the deep result' — the agent needs to be more skeptical of its own reasoning when it argues a stronger option is false.",
