    "reasoning": "The dominant failure (6/8) is misjudging the meta-option ('one of the remaining is correct, but a stronger result can be proven'). The agent needs explicit guidance to treat this option as a serious candidate, not dismiss it by default. The agent also needs to check for subtle flaws in every concrete option before ruling out the meta-option, since these questions are designed so that concrete options often contain a small deliberate weakening or error.",
