        "op": "insert_after",
        "target": "## Theorem-Level Precision",
        "content": "\n### Uncertainty About Theorem Strength\n- If you are not certain of the exact statement of a theorem from the literature, do not fabricate precise claims about what it does or does not prove. Invented theorem knowledge is the leading cause of incorrect strength rankings.\n- When two options differ only in whether an additional property holds (e.g., compatibility with an axiom, full vs. partial equivalence, extra regularity of a function), and you lack definitive knowledge, do not assume the stronger or weaker version by default — flag your uncertainty and consider the meta-option.",
